urse he was right again and  that finally brings us to the situation  with the under display face id on the  iphone 14 pro models when way back last  year he showed us this chart of the 2022  iphone 14 lineup which included the 14  pro and pro max models with under  display face id which is what my entire  video i made a couple of days ago was  based on but now he just came out with a  bombshell leak that completely flips the  script on what he was previously saying  with his firm now believing that the 14  pro models will have both a pill shaped  cutout and the extra circular cutout at  the same time with both of them being  fully visible and if you're wondering  why that extra hole has to be visible  it's likely because apple's tech isn't  quite ready to be put under the display  just yet more specifically the infrared  camera needs to be unobstructed since  it's scanning the ir dots and light from  both the dot projector and flood  illuminator and ray wong on twitter  mentioned an interesting point that  those two models can't be put under the  display because of pixelation since  they're going to be shining through  display pixels and i guess i was wrong  and thinking that it wouldn't matter and  even ross young himself said that  throwing the dot projector under the  display would be too risky so it's  unlikely that apple would be the first  company to introduce under display  infrared technology so because of all of  that it seems like apple is going to  have all of the face id sensors  including the selfie camera completely  unobstructed and that's why we need both  of those hole punch cutouts now getting  back to the actual design we've already  seen quite a few updated renders online  showing what it could potentially look  like and if you're wondering why all of  them are showing the extra circular hole  punch on the right side instead of the  left that's because way back in  september shrimp apple pro mentioned  that the display panel he leaked was  actually a photo taken of the backside  so if you flip it to the front the extra  hole would be on the right and that's  why everyone's renders have it on the  right side but in my personal opinion i  think that the leaked photo was actually  of the front of the display panel  because to me it makes much more sense  for the extra hole on the side to be  used for the selfie camera while all of  the face id sensors will be within the  pill shaped cutouts in the center and  even though ross young believes the hole  on the side is for the dot projector i  would have to disagree at this point in  time so let me explain my point of view  with the iphone 13 smaller notch  redesign apple made a very unusual move  which at the time didn't really make  sense for apparently no reason at all  they decided to move the selfie camera  from the right side of the notch over to  the left side for the first time in the  notches history and this was a really  weird change because apple gave no  reason for this and i personally had to  start reminding myself of the new camera  location on the left side when taking  selfies to be sure that i'm looking  directly into the camera and not off to  the side but now that ross young has  confirmed that the extra circular hole  punch is actually going to be visible  all of the puzzle pieces in my brain  have finally come together and it now  makes total sense if you take that  display panel leak and line it up with  the iphone 13 pros notch the selfie  camera on the 13 almost perfectly lines  up with the extra hole on the leaked  iphone 14 pro display panel so now apple  moving the selfie camera to the left  side finally makes sense now of course i  could be totally wrong about this but i  actually have two very good reasons for  the selfie cam being on the left instead  of within the pill shaped cutout on the  right first of all this would absolutely  be the path of least resistance for  apple since the selfie cam is already on  the left side on the iphone 13 so all  they would essentially have to do on the  14 pro is toss in the new panel with the  hole punch cutouts like we saw in shrimp  apple pros leaks and then take the same  exact glass panels from the iphone 13  lineup and remove the black paint from  the notch area and simply leave a little  bit of black paint around the hole punch  cutouts and bam they're done path of  least resistance and as for the second  reason i want to bring you guys back to  a tweet showing off the updated double  hole punch design one of the features  many believe apple might add back in is  the battery percentage indicator on the  top right of the display and i believe  that's actually much more likely to  happen if the extra hole punch is on the  left side instead because if you really  think about it the only thing on the  left side is the time and potentially a  location icon while the right side has a  cellular data the wi-fi signal and the  battery icon and the only way they'd  have room for the battery percentage is  if the extra hole punch actually goes on  the left so because of all of that i had  renders by shilesh update the previous  render to add in the extra hole on the  left side and in my opinion this looks  pretty great and by the way if you  haven't already followed him on twitter  go ahead and do that to thank him for  his awesome renders and now with that  said there is one more option that some  people on twitter are currently  discussing max weinbach mentioned that  apple could disable the display portion  between the two cutouts to make it a  long pill shaped cutout instead of  having dual cutouts but the problem i  have with this is that it would then  make it completely uncentered and it  would look kind of weird and i don't  think that apple would do this but of  course they could simply slide the whole  thing over to the side to make it  perfectly symmetrical and centered but  then that would mean that the display  panel leak from shrimp apple pro would  have to get tossed out completely since  only the peel shaped cutout is perfectly  centered in his league so in my opinion  i think that apple will go with this  design with two cutouts with the extra  circular cutout on the left side to  allow enough room on the right for the  battery percentage and the reason i  think apple would go with this design  is because it's completely unique and  you will never mistake the iphone 14 pro  for any other android smartphone which  is something that's very important to  apple as we've seen in the past with the  recent macbook pro notch design and of  course the legendary chin on the imac so  with that said if you think i'm  completely wrong about all of this then  let me know down in the comment section  below but if you agree with me then  click the circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one and definitely  check out one of those two right over  there thanks for watching and we'll see  you in the next video  [Music]
 

